Unfortunately, it is not possible to access the local variables of a Python function from the hosting application. The Python interpreter keeps the local variables of a function in its own memory space and does not expose them to the hosting application.

However, you can access the value of the local variables at the time of the exception by extracting them from the trace stack using the following code:

```csharp
for (TraceBackFrame f = frame; f != null; f = f.f\\_back)
{
 // f.f\\_locals contains the local variables of f
}
```

Note that this will only give you the values of the local variables at the time of the exception, not while the function was running. If you need to track the values of local variables over time, you will need to modify the Python code to log or return the values as needed.

